.TH CHARBUF_PRED_GET 3 "2023-04-01" "1.0" "lib/charbuf/charbuf_pred_get"
.SH NAME
charbuf_pred_get \- Get characters from a character buffer based on a predicate
.SH SYNOPSIS
#include <lib/charbuf.h>
#include <lib/stralloc.h>

ssize_t charbuf_pred_get(charbuf *b, stralloc *sa, int (*pred)(int, size_t, void*), void *ptr);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBcharbuf_pred_get\fR function retrieves characters from the character buffer \fBb\fR and appends them to the \fBstralloc\fR buffer \fBsa\fR based on a predicate function \fBpred\fR. The predicate function is called for each character in the buffer, and if it returns non-zero, the character is appended to \fBsa\fR. The function continues to read characters until the predicate returns zero or there are no more characters to read.

This function is useful for extracting a sequence of characters from a buffer that satisfy a certain condition.
.SH ARGUMENTS
\fBb\fR
The character buffer from which to retrieve characters.
\fBsa\fR
The \fBstralloc\fR buffer to which to append the characters.
\fBpred\fR
A predicate function that determines whether a character should be appended.
\fBptr\fR
A pointer to data that will be passed to the predicate function.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The number of characters appended to \fBsa\fR.
.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBcharbuf_pred_get\fR function:
.nf
#include <lib/charbuf.h>
#include <lib/stralloc.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int is_alpha(int c, size_t len, void *ptr) {
    (void)ptr; // Unused
    return (c >= 'a' && c <= 'z') || (c >= 'A' && c <= 'Z');
}

int main() {
    charbuf b;
    charbuf_init(&b);
    charbuf_append(&b, "Hello, world!");

    stralloc sa;
    stralloc_init(&sa);

    charbuf_pred_get(&b, &sa, is_alpha, NULL);

    printf("Extracted characters: %s\n", sa.s);

    charbuf_free(&b);
    stralloc_free(&sa);

    return 0;
}
.ne
.fi
